# SRG-APP-000125-AU-000300  -  CAT III
# The Central Log Server must be configured to back up the log records
# repository at least every seven days onto a different system or system
# component other than the system or component being audited.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000125-AU-000300
group:           V-206458
severity:        low
cat:             CAT III
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       manual
confidence:      derived
revised:         yes
cci:             CCI-001348
control_rev5:    AU-9

contribution:    Where the organization chooses to use them, Splunk can place a second copy
                 of the indexed records off the indexing instance through a frozen archive
                 destination (coldToFrozenDir or coldToFrozenScript), remote store-backed
                 indexes (remotePath), or index replication in a cluster, and the assessor
                 records which is in use as evidence rather than as a pass condition.

external:        The seven-day backup schedule, the backup tool and the medium -
                 SPLK-CL-000250 assigns all three to the operating system backup tool or
                 another approved tool
external:        Confirmation that the destination is a different system or component,
                 which the application cannot establish about a path or endpoint handed to
                 it

manual_reason:   The benchmark authority implements this requirement outside the
                 application: SPLK-CL-000250's check is an interview with the system
                 administrator and its fix directs "the underlying OS backup tools, or
                 another approved backup tool". Splunk has optional levers that place a
                 second copy off the indexing instance, but none that the authority
                 requires, so any condition over them fails a deployment that is backed up
                 exactly as directed.

citation:        server.conf [clustering] replication_factor min 2 is removed:
                 server.conf.spec:2929-2935 makes the setting valid only for "mode=manager"
                 with a default of 3, so a single-instance indexer and a cluster peer alike
                 have no such setting and would be failed for not running a feature the
                 requirement never asks for. coldToFrozenDir non_empty is removed for the
                 same class of error: it fails a stock install whose backups are taken with
                 the operating system tool SPLK-CL-000250 names. Because conditions are
                 ANDed, the pair also demanded index clustering and a frozen archive at the
                 same time, which no single deployment shape satisfies.
finding:         No backup of the log records repository onto a different system or
                 component is in place; the application's optional off-instance copy levers
                 are not a substitute for the backup process the requirement names.
